  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A farm pen contains pigs and chickens. A farmer counts twenty-three heads and seventy legs. How many pigs and chickens are in the pen?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "12 pigs and 11 chickens.",
      "worked": "Let $p$ be the number of pigs and $c$ the number of chickens.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}p+c&=23 &&(1)\\\\4p+2c&=70 &&(2)\\\\2p+2c&=46 &&2\\times(1)\\\\2p&=24 &&(2)-2\\times(1)\\\\p&=12\\\\12+c&=23\\\\c&=11\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are 12 pigs and 11 chickens. Check: $12+11=23$ heads and $4(12)+2(11)=70$ legs.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
